35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The late-turn pool is empty. We are using overtime to cover the final departures and the overnight works.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The pilots from eight years ago actually worked. The ferry payment trial closed without technical faults.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The committee minutes show the ferry and rail back offices never agreed common passenger data terms.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The capital ledger still carries a ring-fenced construction balance from a lapsed grant.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The audits show passengers lose most minutes waiting for connections, not paying. The timed runs confirm the surface route is slow.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, if the pilots worked, why did we not scale them? I suspect the crew shortage stopped us.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the accessibility records show two lane-priority stretches were returned to mixed traffic. We gave up on them.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the pre-war shells are a trap. Bidders price heavy contingency because of unrecorded voids.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, that explains the contingency. But the ticketing fees are eating the paving budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, if the fees are high, we should fix the connection waits first. That is where the time goes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"I cannot promise new services if the maintenance contract is already stretched. The lift crew has spare capacity, though.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,The ferry pilot proves the tech works. We just need to stop ignoring the closure reports.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The roadway consents are already delegated to the authority. That is a clear path.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,The ring-fenced balance is for construction. We can use it for the ferry without touching the operating subsidy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,The surface route is the real problem. The timed runs show it is a third slower. We need to fix that.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am worried about the crew. If we add more services, the late-turn pool will collapse.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I am confident the ferry pilot is the right move. It is proven and the money is there.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am cautious about the pre-war shells. The ground risks are too high. The roadway is safer.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am relieved the ring-fenced funds are available. It avoids the subsidy argument.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I am excited about the ferry. It addresses the real bottleneck and uses the available funds.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
